=== discard-switch-implementation-notes.md ===
# v37 discard-switch implementation evidence

Date: 6 November 2026, America/Toronto. Offline local controller/service evidence only.

## Confirmed defect and narrow correction

`ConversationPreviewStore.resolveSwitchDecision("discard")` previously called
`discardActiveChanges()` for every source thread. That method returns immediately
when the thread has never been saved. Switching dropped its composer text and
cancelled work, but left the old UI transcript and service record in memory; the
controller could reopen the old identifier. This is in-memory retention and a
controller reopening defect. No unsaved-thread button in the saved list,
participant exposure, or live-provider disclosure was observed.

The new branch matches existing finish-discard behavior: a source with a saved
snapshot still cancels work and restores that snapshot; a never-saved source uses
the existing `deleteThread` lifecycle. This cancels pending store/service work,
purges the service's record and associated caches, and invalidates its old
lifecycle binding. The already captured pending target is then selected by the
existing `performSwitch`. Cancel and Save branches are unchanged.

Only two repository files are owned/changed by this task:

- `src/lib/ai/conversation/preview/store.ts`: branch plus explanatory comment.
- `src/lib/ai/conversation/__tests__/preview-discard-switch.test.ts`: 18 new cases.

## New regression coverage

Six actual-service cases exercise completed, scheduled-before-dispatch, and
already-dispatched turns, each switching to a new or saved destination. The real
service uses its existing local mock provider, deliberately configured to ignore
abort so late completion must be rejected by the actual service/store boundaries.
Tests verify removal of the UI/service record, refusal to reopen/export old
authority, invalidation of the old lifecycle binding, removal of synthetic draft,
derived-context and confirmed-excerpt canaries, preservation of unrelated and
destination saved snapshots/service content, and isolation of the next assembled
mock-provider request. Operational target generation changes are legitimate;
preservation checks compare saved/content state and lifecycle identity.

Six no-service rollback cases cover completed, scheduled and draft-only sources,
again with both target kinds and deliberate late scheduled callback execution.
Six preservation controls, divided between actual-service and no-service stores,
cover saved-snapshot restoration, exact Cancel preservation and later pending-turn
completion, and Save refusing an unsent draft/pending reply/simulated failure
before a successful deliberate Save-and-switch. Final switch state checks include
empty draft, selected draft owner, null pending switch/transcript and voice off.

These tests inspect live service caches; they do not claim to erase detached
snapshots or requests already returned to and retained by a caller. Synthetic
excerpt insertion calls the existing service method only as a test fixture; no
private writing is retrieved and no content/sharing policy is changed.

## Commands, original diagnostics and correction

Initial accidental invocation used the available Bun executable directly on
Vitest. Collection failed before tests with `z.enum` undefined in `grants.ts`.
The unmodified diagnostic is `discard-switch-baseline.log`; this is a runner
invocation diagnostic, not a regression result. No dependency or application
change was made to address it.

The established Node command is:

```sh
node node_modules/vitest/vitest.mjs run src/lib/ai/conversation/__tests__/preview-discard-switch.test.ts --maxWorkers=2 --testTimeout=15000
```

- Before source fix: **12 failed, 6 passed**, all 18 executed; every failure was
  the intended assertion that the never-saved old thread must be absent.
  `discard-switch-baseline-node.log` preserves the original failures.
- After narrow source fix: **18 passed, zero skipped**.
  `discard-switch-fixed.log` preserves the result.
- New test file passes full ESLint: `discard-switch-test-lint.log`.
- Source plus test full lint initially reports 10 formatting-only findings in
  untouched store locations: `discard-switch-lint-initial.log`. Passing the
  unchanged v36 store bytes to ESLint with the same current filename reproduces
  the same 10 findings: `discard-switch-lint-baseline.log`. Unrelated source was
  deliberately not reformatted. Source semantic lint with only the Prettier
  formatting rule disabled is recorded separately in
  `discard-switch-source-lint.log`.

Root/other agent owns the final affected regression suite, TypeScript and build
validation; this note does not invent their results. Reviewer performs a separate
read and rerun.

