=== discard-independent-review.md ===
# Independent review — never-saved preview discard and switch

6 November 2026. Read-only triage began at verified GitHub checkpoint `589e594b8ad33c99176fe6fd367ce7297f5ba6c5`, then the fresh v37 workspace was authorized for the narrow fix. No browser, Auth, model, voice provider, connected SQL or setup probe was used.

## Reproduced baseline defect

The actual existing `ConversationPreviewStore`, `ConversationService` and canned local provider reproduce this sequence:

1. Create a never-saved thread and complete one fictional exchange.
2. Request a new conversation: the store returns `needs-decision`.
3. Choose `resolveSwitchDecision("discard")`: it returns success.
4. The prior thread still has two UI messages and two service events, and its synthetic canary remains in the live service record. A direct controller request to reopen the old ID succeeds and restores that canary.

The UI's existing switch dialog promises that Discard & continue discards unsent text and unsaved changes. However, `resolveSwitchDecision` called `discardActiveChanges`, which returned immediately for a null saved snapshot. The separate existing finish-discard path already deletes a never-saved thread. Existing preview and service integration tests covered discard-switch from saved snapshots, leaving this distinct branch uncovered.

This is retained discarded content and authority inside the local preview's live stores. It is **not** evidence of participant exposure or a live-provider leak: the UI lists only saved conversations, so the controller reopening result does not imply an available old-thread UI button. Previously returned snapshots and captured provider requests are separate references; deleting current records cannot erase those external copies.

The scratch-only runnable baseline diagnostic and result are `baseline-triage-discard-repro.cjs` and `baseline-triage-discard-repro.json`. Pass a repository path as the script's first argument to select the source. Its assertions deliberately describe the baseline defect, not desired post-fix behavior. `baseline-discard-source-hashes.json` records that the inspected v36 files exactly matched the fresh v37 baseline before edits. The script uses actual source via esbuild, the existing node-test browser-init seam and one canned provider dispatch; it does not execute UI code in a browser or create persistent data.

## Review scope

The narrow repair should reuse existing deletion for the never-saved branch and retain the prior saved-snapshot branch. Review covers removal of the discarded thread's current UI/service record and grants/turns, invalidation of its lifecycle binding, refusal to reopen/export that missing record, cancellation of queued or late work, final navigation/draft/voice state, and preservation of saved destinations and unrelated saved content. A reopened destination may legitimately change operational generation while its content and lifecycle association stay intact.

Deleted-target/self-open controller edge paths, unrelated UI navigation redesign, new policy/content, persistence, provider lifecycle implementation and runtime wiring are outside this fix. Existing `deleteThread` and `performSwitch` already supply active voice cleanup and pending-transcript clearing; existing P3a repair regressions cover their voice/cache boundaries. No duplicate independent test fixture is needed unless review identifies a distinct new defect.

## Final checks

The final narrow source change is approved with no remaining blocker found. The never-saved discard branch calls the existing `deleteThread(active.id)`, while saved snapshots keep their prior cancel/restore behavior. The unchanged deletion path aborts queued work, invalidates voice, removes the service record and its owned grants/turns, and clears active local draft state. The existing switch path then opens the selected destination and clears pending switch/transcript state. No application component, policy, content, service implementation, SQL or runtime wiring changed.

Independently ran the final new regression file through actual Node/Vitest: **18/18 passed, one file, zero skips**, exit 0 in 3.29 seconds. The local provider cases exercise completed work, cancellation before dispatch and deliberately late replies that ignore abort, for both new and saved destinations. The no-service cases and Cancel/Save/saved-snapshot controls also pass. The run used no browser or connected service. Evidence: `discard-independent-focused.log` and `discard-independent-focused.json`.

Frozen source hashes were verified before and after the independent run:

- `src/lib/ai/conversation/preview/store.ts`: `1607c294265910f464e4c76c92b34d336918dac83ca5159dc555f519d4650485`
- `src/lib/ai/conversation/__tests__/preview-discard-switch.test.ts`: `28a7f75f26f14fbd8f09584c80b13c7cd5101c59596c52bc9a2a8a184b5ac5dd`

Compared all 455 prior `src` files with the verified v36 source: the only changed prior file is `preview/store.ts`, and the only new source file is the focused regression file. No separate independent test file was added; the new 18-case fixture and existing deletion/voice regression coverage already address the narrow change without a duplicate harness.

The implementation author's first Bun attempt failed during collection and is not a functional test result. The preserved actual Node baseline is 12 failed removal assertions and six passing controls; the repaired result is 18/18. The ten reported formatting findings are also present in the unchanged baseline store; they were not repaired in this narrow batch. Full lint of the new test passes, and source semantic lint with the existing formatting rule disabled passes; this is not a claim of clean full-file formatting lint.

The parent reports the affected six-file regression run passed 217/217 with zero skips, plus strict TypeScript, production build and scoped semantic lint. Those checks are separate from this independent 18-case rerun and are not a newly executed full repository or SQL suite. Browser accessibility modes and all 37 native PostgreSQL cases remain separately prepared and unrun. No visual, screen-reader, device, hosted Auth or provider acceptance is established.

